cc 1.1.19..1.1.31: add the PowerPC Darwin targets to the macOS architecture table of apple_flags(), as
cc@1.0.85..1.1.33.patch did (P43). That patch carried ONE line of context on each side so a single
file could span 1.0.85..1.1.33; GNU patch's default fuzz (2) may then drop the context entirely and
insert the two match arms at the hunk's recorded line (2720) instead of at the table: in cc 1.0.98
that is inside the `cmd.args.extend([..])` array of the Mac Catalyst branch, and mrustc reports
`lib.rs:2721:30 error:0: Unexpected token TOK_FATARROW, expected TOK_SQUARE_CLOSE` (hunt-rs 3.0.0,
2026-11-01). Replaced by three files with three lines of context each, split where the surrounding
lines changed (1.1.19 added `| "arm64e"` to the 64-bit arm, 1.1.32 replaced `if is_mac` by `if target.os == "macos"`). Dry-run `patch -p1 -t -N -F0` on every crates.io release 1.0.85-1.2.5: exact
application on exactly this range, rejected elsewhere. Applying crate patches with -F0 in the
PortGroup would turn any future misplacement into a loud failure.

--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -2718,6 +2718,8 @@
 
         let arch = if is_mac {
             match arch_str {
+                "powerpc" => AppleArchSpec::Device("-m32"),
+                "powerpc64" => AppleArchSpec::Device("-m64"),
                 "i686" => AppleArchSpec::Device("-m32"),
                 "x86_64" | "x86_64h" | "aarch64" | "arm64e" => AppleArchSpec::Device("-m64"),
                 _ => {
